      "ordinal": 8,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "4.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "Chainmail Aventails have been part of armor since the earliest helmets. By the 14th and 15th centuries, it was almost impossible to have a helmet without a chainmail Aventail.\n\nThey are Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\n\nBook of the Queen - 1410/1414 - France Wallace Collection - 1390/1410 - UK",
