    {
      "ordinal": 18,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "6.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "Fabric Aventail, often displayed over chainmail Aventail, serves decorative purposes. They may feature multi-colored designs, decorative stitching, embroidery, and coats of arms. While this type of Aventail is documented by sources from the 14th century, there is no evidence of fabric Aventail later on. The mail elements present with other 15th-century helmets like Barbutes and Sallets are not Aventails but mail standards/collars.\n\nThey are Approved for 14th century and Transitional armors.\nThey are for 15th century armors.\n\nChurch of St Georges, Schenna - 1380/1400 - Italy Runkelstein Castle, Ritten- 1395/1405 - Italy",
      "page_from": 9,
      "page_to": 9,
      "stable_key": "aventails:6.1",
