    {
      "ordinal": 19,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "6.2",
      "title": "Specific Requirements",
      "body": "Fabric Aventail must:\n\n● follow the General Requirements (see Section 3 above),\n● consist of at least one layer of fabric, attached to the helmet using the same suspension method as other aventails (see Section 7 below),\n● conform to the “Textiles and Leather” document,\n● include at least one of the approved decoration methods, such as:\n○ Multi-color base (at least 2 distinct colors), ○ Embroidery, ○ Stitching, ○ Stamp-printing.\nDecorations must be inspired by medieval images and not be offensive.\nAny additional plates must be concealed when standing.\n\nIt is recommended to sew the fabric aventail to the pelerine.",
