      "ordinal": 23,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "7.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "From the first bascinets of the 14th century until the late armets, Aventails were attached to helmets using a suspension system made of vervelles and leather. This system was used from the 14th to the 16th centuries.\n\nIt is Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\n\nBascinet Royal Armouries, Leeds - 1380/1400 - Italy",
