    {
      "ordinal": 25,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "7.3",
      "title": "Specific Requirements",
      "body": "The suspension system consists of vervelles, a piece of leather, and thread.\n\n● Vervelles These are metal components with a hole, allowing threads (metal or leather) to pass through.\n\n● Leather Piece The aventail (chainmail neck guard) is attached to a leather piece, which can be riveted or sewn.\n\n● Thread\n\n● The thread, made of either metal or leather (or materials that replicate their look), passes through the vervelles to secure the leather piece to the helmet.\n\nAlternative method for fabric Aventail: the Aventail can be sewn directly to the helmet’s edge.",
      "page_from": 13,
